{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "Elias blinked awake, expecting the familiar, slightly warped texture of his bedroom ceiling, but instead found a grid of perfect, glowing blue squares stretching endlessly above him. He scrambled to his feet, only to discover that his movements felt unnaturally stiff, as if his limbs were being guided by an invisible script rather than his own will. When he reached for his bedside lamp, it didn't clatter to the floor; it simply vanished with a soft digital chime and a floating text bubble that read, \"Item Collected.\" Panic surged through him as he looked out the window, seeing the sky rendered in low-resolution clouds that looped in a three-second cycle, while distant mountains jaggedly shifted geometry every time he blinked.\n\n***\n\nDesperate for answers, Elias ran toward the door, but the hallway stretched infinitely, a corridor of repeating textures that refused to end no matter how fast he sprinted. A translucent menu hovered in his peripheral vision, displaying his health bar, inventory slots, and a quest marker that pulsed insistently toward a door that hadn't existed yesterday. He tried to scream for a real person, but the sound that escaped his throat was a pre-recorded audio clip of a generic \"Help!\" that played on a loop, detached from his true emotions. As the world began to flicker and reload around him, Elias realized with a sinking horror that he was no longer the player controlling the story, but merely a character trapped in an endless, unskippable cutscene.", "logprobs": [{"token": "E", "logprob": -0.3487009}, {"token": "lias", "logprob": -8.869565e-05}, {"token": " blinked", "logprob": -0.9694809}, {"token": " awake", "logprob": -1.949431}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.6934858}, {"token": " expecting", "logprob": -0.16787076}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -9.179157e-06}, {"token": " familiar", "logprob": -0.21685265}, {"token": ","